@@ -70,6 +70,21 @@ The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.log` methods offers the same capabilities as pr
 To help with debugging, the log() method has a ``log_locals`` parameter. If you set this to ``True``, Rich will display a table of local variables where the method was called.
 
 
+Low level output
+----------------
+
+The :meth:`~rich.console.Console.out` method is a lower-level alternative to print and log. It converts each object to a string, joins them with ``sep``, and writes the result followed by ``end``. It does the following:
+
+- Writes plain text without pretty printing.
+- Does not wrap, crop, or apply markup or emoji code replacement.
+- Applies a basic ``style`` if one is given.
+- Highlights output by default. Pass ``highlight=False`` to disable highlighting, or ``highlight=None`` to use the console's highlight setting.
+
+Here's an example::
+
+    >>> console.out("foo", [1, 2], "[bold]bar[/bold]", sep=", ")
+
+
